From 22c4b520a2e42605654561194338d9c40711ac67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tommy <tommy@pham.cc>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 03:13:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 62/65] Run-ahead (TEKKEN4_RUNAHEAD=1|2, default off) on the
 rollback snapshots

Per host frame the real frame runs hidden (no draw, no VU1, no present; IOP
live), the machine is captured, N speculative frames run with the same input
(IOP in the snapshot, muted; the last one draws), their picture is latched
for the presenter and the machine is restored. Host deadlines move N frames
earlier once, so the picture of frame k+N shows when frame k would have.
The scheduler gets a boundary wrapper so the game's own boundary hook (the
rollback driver) only sees real frames. Off in netplay and the rollback
test/selfnet modes. Speculative pad reads do not consume latched taps.
Checked: rollback-measure state hashes of 4377 real frames identical to a
run without run-ahead (scripted Story fight with fuzz input).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
